# Issue #1175 R1175-4 — held-out routing probes, code lanes.
#
# One probe per block — the precedence lane it exercises (a handler row of
# data/seed/handler-precedence.lino, a slug of data/seed/intent-routing.lino,
# or an extra lane declared in budget.lino), the prompt language, the intent
# the system SHOULD answer, and the prompt. A quoted value doubles an inner
# quote and writes a newline as \n.
#
# `js_misroute <intent>` / `rust_misroute <intent>` record a probe the browser
# worker / the native solver answers wrongly today, naming the intent it
# answers instead; both are measured, never `unverified` (issue 1173 R3). Both
# are ratchets with ceilings in budget.lino — a listed probe that starts
# answering correctly fails the test until its line is removed and the ceiling
# lowered, one that moves to another intent fails until its line is updated,
# and a new misroute fails outright. `rust_intent` names a designed runtime difference (the
# native chat surface refuses tool execution outside Agent mode).
# `adversarial true` marks prose that surface-matches another lane.
routing_probes
  probe p004
    lane agent_suggestion
    language en
    intent agent_suggestion
    prompt "git status"
  probe p005
    lane agent_suggestion
    language en
    intent agent_suggestion
